From: NXRS project maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] rp23xx: adapt CYW43439 transport to the pinned baseline

The pinned revision predates the move of debug.h under nuttx/. Use its
existing public header. Also store positive errno when setup fails:
bcmf_gspi_initialize returns a negative errno, not a libc errno value.
Otherwise board bring-up's -errno would mistakenly report a positive result.

These are separate from the accepted transport backport so its upstream
implementation remains identifiable. The errno correction can be proposed
upstream independently; the header path change is baseline-specific.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_cyw43439.c b/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_cyw43439.c
--- a/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_cyw43439.c
+++ b/arch/arm/src/rp23xx/rp23xx_cyw43439.c
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
 #include <nuttx/config.h>
 
 #include <stdio.h>
-#include <nuttx/debug.h>
+#include <debug.h>
 #include <errno.h>
 
 #include <nuttx/kmalloc.h>
@@ -854,7 +854,7 @@ gspi_dev_t *rp23xx_cyw_setup(uint8_t gpio_on,
       kmm_free(gspi);
       kmm_free(rp_io);
 
-      set_errno(err);
+      set_errno(-err);
       return NULL;
     }
 
